// The bestiary — the creatures that live the world's biomes. Each species favours
// certain Holdridge formations and a biotemperature band; outside them it cannot
// thrive. `size` scales how much it eats and burns; `fecundity` its breeding rate;
// `gregarious` how tightly it herds (0 = solitary, ~1 = dense herd / pack). `form`
// is its body plan / gait (Strider | Lumberer | Prowler | Critter | Serpent |
// Drifter), which the renderer builds its procedural shape and animation from.
// Authored otherworldly to suit the dream-purgatory: nothing here walks the waking Earth.
//
// Fields: name, diet (Herbivore | Carnivore), form, habitat (formation names:
// desert, tundra, grassland, shrubland, forest, rainforest), min_temp/max_temp
// (°C biotemperature it tolerates), size, fecundity, gregarious, color (r,g,b).
